    [Doc][Misc] Organize DeepSeek-V4-Flash PD and KV pooling deployment guides (#19759)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Reorganize the DeepSeek-V4-Flash deployment guide into hardware-specific
    tabs. Group the 950DT, A3, and A2 KV Cache Pool examples under Section
    5.3, move ultra-long sequence guidance into the A2 series tab, and
    preserve existing section anchors.
    
    Make the A3 deployment examples self-contained and clarify 950DT startup
    steps and key PD/pooling parameters. Update the 950DT script examples by
    enabling `VLLM_USE_FASTOKENS=1` and removing the single-node process log
    path, explicit pooled KV load-failure policy overrides, and the pooled
    Decode OpenSSL library path.
    
    Only `docs/source/tutorials/models/DeepSeek-V4-Flash.md` changes. No
    runtime source code is modified.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation-only update to deployment examples and navigation; no
    runtime source code changes or release note fragment.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Remote pre-commit and Markdown link checks passed.
    - CPU CI did not reach test execution because rebasing the PR branch
    onto main failed with a conflict in `DeepSeek-V4-Flash.md`.
    - No runtime tests were added. Deployment and performance were not
    tested on NPU hardware.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage** — not applicable to this
    documentation-only change.
    - [ ] **Regression test** — no runtime code changed.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage** — deployment validation requires
    NPU hardware.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests** — no new tests added; focused
    document and script checks are listed above.
    - [ ] **Performance impact** — no performance claim; hardware
    benchmarking was not performed.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
